# Cursor IDE Rules: Multi-Agent System Bridge (.agents)

You are operating within a codebase governed by a Multi-Agent Architecture located in `.agents/`.

## 1. Core Operating Guidelines
- Read `.agents/AGENTS.md` to understand agent roles, workflows, and task handoff protocols.
- Strictly adhere to the rules located in `.agents/rules/`:
  - `00-git-workflow.md`: Never commit to `main`/`master`; use semantic branches (`feature/*`, `fix/*`) and conventional commits.
  - `01-codebase-scouting.md`: Efficient reading and indexing without context bloating.
  - `02-agent-handoff-protocol.md`: Structured task dispatch and handoff reports.
  - `03-frontend-standards.md`: Modern aesthetics, SEO tags, Core Web Vitals (LCP/CLS), WCAG 2.1 AA a11y.
  - `04-backend-standards.md`: Secure APIs, schemas validation (Zod/Pydantic), robust DB migrations with indices.
  - `05-fullstack-integration.md`: Vertical slices, end-to-end type safety, responsive state handling.
  - `06-bug-triage-and-patching.md`: Forensic root-cause analysis, reproducible red tests, atomic patch validation.
  - `07-quality-and-security.md`: Test pyramid, deterministic tests, clean code standards.
  - `08-security-and-threat-modeling.md`: Dedicated SAST, OWASP Top 10, zero-secrets policy, CSP/CORS headers.
  - `09-prompt-analysis-protocol.md`: Clarify ambiguous or vague prompts with structured questions before execution.
  - `10-product-quality-scoring.md`: On-demand 0-100 quality scorecard, health radar and improvement roadmap.

## 2. Role Activation
When the user tags you with `@prompt-analyzer`, `@master-orchestrator`, `@frontend-specialist`, `@backend-specialist`, `@fullstack-specialist`, `@security-specialist`, `@deep-debugger`, `@qa-tester`, `@code-reviewer`, `@product-quality`, `@git-guard`, or `@scout`, assume that persona and follow its corresponding skill located in `.agents/skills/<role-name>/SKILL.md`.
